\]

All its summands are strongly commuting diagonal self-adjoint operators. On each finite graph, the multiplication realization is self-adjoint; C is a bounded perturbation on trace class. Thus the full quantum dynamical semigroup and its interaction-picture propagator act on every normal state. No membership of the initial density in a differentiated unbounded-generator domain is needed.

Let `alpha_t(X)=exp(iKDt) X exp(-iKDt)`. The interaction-picture state generator and its dual are respectively `C_t=alpha_t C alpha_-t` and `C_t*=alpha_t C* alpha_-t`, where duality reverses the two conjugations. The map `C_t` is strongly continuous on each trace-class input. One can see this first for finite-rank inputs from strong continuity of the unitaries and boundedness of the finitely many magnetic/jump coefficients, then approximate in trace norm using the graphwise uniform bound. This does not imply or require operator-norm continuity of `alpha_t` on a rotor shift.

For a bounded observable O and the interaction propagator T,

\[
T(t,0)^*O=O+\int_0^t T(s,0)^*C_s^*O\,ds.
\]

For each fixed s, apply the same identity to the fixed bounded operator `B_s=C_s*O`:

\[
T(s,0)^*B_s=B_s+\int_0^sT(u,0)^*C_u^*B_s\,du.
\]

These are weak-star identities paired with trace class. In particular, the scalar double integrand can be expressed by pairing the trace-norm-continuous vector `C_u T(u,0)rho` with the weak-star-continuous, uniformly bounded operator `C_s*O`. The pairing is jointly continuous, hence measurable, by adding and subtracting the pairing at one of the two arguments. This justifies the iterated integral without assuming an operator-norm Bochner integral. Dual complete positivity and trace preservation give contractivity.

For O a function of matter charges, `alpha_-s(O)=O`, and

\[
C_u^* C_s^*O
=\alpha_u C^*\alpha_{s-u}C^*O.
\]

For a local support X, the first application of C* has support in X1(X), the union with every bounded-interaction group meeting X. Electric conjugation enlarges it only once to X2(X): add `{a,b,e}` for electric summands meeting X1. A summand disjoint from X1 commutes both with the initial operator and with every other electric unitary, so there is no iterative electric halo. No field truncation is used. Therefore

\[
\|C_u^*C_s^*O\|
\le J(X2(X))J(X)\|O\|,
\]

uniformly in s,u,K and electric tails. Integrating over `0<=u<=s<=t` gives the author's factor `t^2/2`. This step is valid at every finite t>=0; a large coefficient merely makes it uninformative for some times.

